    <item>
      <title>Shared Runners</title>
      <link>https://ampcode.com/news/shared-runners</link>
      <description>
        <![CDATA[<p>You can now share a <a href="/docs/cli/runners">runner</a> with your workspace. Start it with <code>--share</code> and everyone in your workspace can start threads on that machine from ampcode.com.</p>
<p><picture class="responsive-picture" style="--image-width:1824px"><source media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" type="image/avif" srcset="https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/shared-runners-picker-light.f218556a.768w.avif 768w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/shared-runners-picker-light.f218556a.1440w.avif 1440w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/shared-runners-picker-light.f218556a.1824w.avif 1824w" sizes="(min-width: 1307px) 660px, (min-width: 1024px) 50.5vw, (min-width: 716px) 660px, calc(100vw - 56px)"><source media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" srcset="https://static.ampcode.com/news/shared-runners-picker-light.png?v=2" /><source type="image/avif" srcset="https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/shared-runners-picker-dark.a5d2919a.768w.avif 768w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/shared-runners-picker-dark.a5d2919a.1440w.avif 1440w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/shared-runners-picker-dark.a5d2919a.1824w.avif 1824w" sizes="(min-width: 1307px) 660px, (min-width: 1024px) 50.5vw, (min-width: 716px) 660px, calc(100vw - 56px)"><img width="1824" height="1185" style="box-shadow: none !important; border: none !important" src="https://static.ampcode.com/news/shared-runners-picker-dark.png?v=2" alt="The new thread composer on ampcode.com with the location picker open. Under Runners is your own devbox. Under Shared Runners are gpu-runner, shared by Allison, and macos-builder, shared by Monty, each with its owner's avatar and running-thread count." decoding="sync" data-lightbox-src="https://static.ampcode.com/news/shared-runners-picker-dark.png?v=2"></picture></p>
<p>If you have a machine with GPUs, a Mac that&#39;s used to build and sign the iOS app, or a dev box in a specific network, you can now set it up and the whole team can spawn agents on it:</p>
<pre><code class="language-shell-session">$ amp --no-tui --runner-id macos-builder --share
</code></pre>
<p>Everyone in your workspace now sees it in the picker under <strong>Shared Runners</strong>.</p>
<p>With <a href="/docs/cli/runners#secrets-env-vars"><code>--amp-env</code></a>, a shared runner gets the workspace and project Secrets &amp; Env Vars, but never your personal ones. That applies to your own threads on it too.</p>
<p>We need to offer a word of warning, though: everyone you share with runs code on your machine as you, with your files, your credentials, and your logins. Their threads can also work in the same directories at the same time. So only share a runner with people you&#39;d trust with a shell on that machine. Even better, give the runner a machine of its own. (Better still: use <a href="/what-are-orbs">orbs</a>, so that every thread gets its own machine.)</p>
<p>Workspace admins can <a href="/docs/cli/runners#turn-off-runner-sharing-for-a-workspace">turn off runner sharing</a> in <strong>Member Settings</strong>.</p>
<p>Read more about <a href="/docs/cli/runners#share-a-runner-with-your-workspace">sharing a runner</a> in the runner docs.</p>]]>
      </description>
      <pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Mac App Is Your Runner</title>
      <link>https://ampcode.com/news/the-mac-app-is-your-runner</link>
      <description>
        <![CDATA[<p>The <a href="/app">Amp app for macOS</a> now starts a <a href="/docs/cli/runners">runner</a> for you. You no longer need <code>amp --no-tui</code> open in a terminal to run threads on your Mac.</p>
<p><picture class="responsive-picture" style="--image-width:1504px"><source type="image/avif" srcset="https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/mac-app-runner-settings.2dbc6a0f.768w.avif 768w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/mac-app-runner-settings.2dbc6a0f.1440w.avif 1440w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/mac-app-runner-settings.2dbc6a0f.1504w.avif 1504w" sizes="(min-width: 1307px) 660px, (min-width: 1024px) 50.5vw, (min-width: 716px) 660px, calc(100vw - 56px)"><img width="1504" height="1668" style="box-shadow: none !important; border: none !important; max-width: min(560px, 100%)" src="https://static.ampcode.com/news/mac-app-runner-settings.png" alt="The Runner tab in the Amp app's settings on macOS. Use This Mac as a Runner is switched on, the status says Running with 3 folders and 2 threads, the runner name is hamishs-macbook-pro, Keep This Mac Awake is switched on, and the Folders list shows amp, sandcastle, and marketing-site." decoding="sync" data-lightbox-src="https://static.ampcode.com/news/mac-app-runner-settings.png"></picture></p>
<p>Open <strong>App Settings…</strong> (⌘⇧,), go to <strong>Runner</strong>, and click <strong>+</strong> to add a folder or one of your projects. Start a thread and your Mac is right there in the picker, marked <strong>This Mac</strong>. You can also pick it when you start a thread from ampcode.com, your phone, or Puck.</p>
<p><picture class="responsive-picture" style="--image-width:1824px"><source media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" type="image/avif" srcset="https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-light.6e7b5e39.768w.avif 768w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-light.6e7b5e39.1440w.avif 1440w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-light.6e7b5e39.1824w.avif 1824w" sizes="(min-width: 1307px) 660px, (min-width: 1024px) 50.5vw, (min-width: 716px) 660px, calc(100vw - 56px)"><source media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" srcset="https://static.ampcode.com/news/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-light.png" /><source type="image/avif" srcset="https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-dark.ccdd4429.768w.avif 768w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-dark.ccdd4429.1440w.avif 1440w, https://static.ampcode.com/news/responsive/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-dark.ccdd4429.1824w.avif 1824w" sizes="(min-width: 1307px) 660px, (min-width: 1024px) 50.5vw, (min-width: 716px) 660px, calc(100vw - 56px)"><img width="1824" height="1033" style="box-shadow: none !important; border: none !important" src="https://static.ampcode.com/news/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-dark.png" alt="The new thread composer in the Amp app with the prompt Make amp an iPhone Duo app and the ultra mode. The runner picker is open, and hamishs-macbook-pro is selected with a This Mac capsule and a MacBook icon. Below it is hamishs-dgx-spark, another runner, with no capsule." loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-lightbox-src="https://static.ampcode.com/news/your-mac-is-now-a-runner-composer-dark.png"></picture></p>
<h2>No More Sleeping on the Job</h2>
<p><strong>Keep This Mac Awake</strong> stops your Mac from going to sleep while the runner is on and the Mac is plugged in, so you can still start threads on it after you walk away. The screen still turns off and locks. On battery, or when you close the lid, your Mac sleeps as usual.</p>
<p>Read more in the <a href="/docs/macos-and-ios/runner">runner docs</a>.</p>]]>
      </description>
